Both files open without a problem. What does this code do?
```
FILE *in = fopen("old.txt", "r");
FILE *out = fopen("new.txt", "w");
int ch;
while ((ch = fgetc(in)) != EOF)
    fputc(ch, out);
fclose(in);
fclose(out);
```

